ThinkBrake ( Song et al., 2026 ) ends the CoT at a sentence boundary when the margin between the most likely next token other than </think> and </think> , on the temperature-scaled logits, is at most τ 	au . Its paper uses τ = 0.1 	au{=}0.1 for every Qwen3 model. The paper does not say in which state the margin is read. Its only released code (for its tool-use benchmark) appends a period and a single newline to each prefix and reads </think> there, which is the state in which Qwen3 closes its CoT on its own. In our runs every natural close follows a single-newline token, whereas a sentence inside the CoT mostly ends in a blank-line token, after which </think> is never near the top. Read in the state the model actually wrote, the rule therefore does not fire. We therefore follow the released code. At every sentence boundary, a token that ends a sentence and is followed by whitespace, or a token that ends with a newline, the sentence’s last token is replaced by its single-newline form ( .

