 ) and the margin is read there. Where the rule fires, the run keeps its CoT up to that sentence, followed by the single newline, </think> and a freshly sampled answer. Like DEER, ThinkBrake is evaluated on the stored plain-decoding runs. It removes 21% of the thinking tokens over the seven benchmarks at a cost of 2.3 points: 37% on GPQA-Diamond and 44% on LiveCodeBench, where it costs 2.0 and 4.7 points, and 3–4% on the five others (Table 7 ). The paper reports 4–6% fewer thinking tokens on AIME 2024 and 2025 and 20% on GPQA-Diamond for Qwen3-32B with a 16k budget.

